jpg","width":1405,"height":1988,"method":"openai-vision:gpt-5.4-mini","status":"complete"},{"number":2,"image":"/repeat-v2/assets/083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7/page-2.jpg","width":1405,"height":1988,"method":"openai-vision:gpt-5.4-mini","status":"complete"}],"questions":[{"id":"083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7-q-1","number":"1A","markdown":"A survey conducted in a slum locality reveals the following information as classified below:\n\n| Income per day (Rs.) | Under 10 | 10-20 | 20-30 | 30-40 | 40-50 |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| Number of persons | 20 | 45 | 115 | 210 | 115 |\n\nEstimate the probable number of persons in the income group 20-25.","marks":4,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7/q-1-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,570,1405,219],"id":"083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7-q-1-diagram-1","caption":"Classified table of income per day and number of persons (original source region)"}],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7/q-1-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,570,1405,219]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7-q-2","number":"1B","markdown":"Solve $\\dfrac{dy}{dx} = \\dfrac{y^4 + 2y}{4x - x y^3 - 2y^4}$.","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7/q-2-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,781,1405,130]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7-q-3","number":"1C","markdown":"From the data given below, compute $\\left(\\dfrac{dy}{dx}\\right)_{x=3}$ and $\\left(\\dfrac{d^2 y}{dx^2}\\right)_{x=-2}$.\n\n| $x$ | -2 | -1 | 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| $y$ | 0 | 1 | 6 | 24 | 60 | 120 |","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7/q-3-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,903,1405,228],"id":"083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7-q-3-diagram-1","caption":"Data table for x and y values (original source region)"}],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7/q-3-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,903,1405,228]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7-q-4","number":"2A","markdown":"Using Runge Kutta method of fourth order, solve $y' = x + y^2$ with $y(0)=1$ at $x=0.2$ in steps of length $h=0.1$.","marks":4,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7/q-4-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1122,1405,127]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7-q-5","number":"2B","markdown":"Solve $(3y^4 + 3x^2y^2)\\,dx + (x^3y - 3xy^3)\\,dy = 0$.","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7/q-5-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1241,1405,100]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7-q-6","number":"2C","markdown":"Find the approximate value of $\\int_0^{\\pi/2} \\sqrt{\\cos \\theta}\\, d\\theta$ using Simpson’s $1/3^{\\mathrm{rd}}$ rule by dividing $[0, \\pi/2]$ into 6 equal parts.","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7/q-6-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1333,1405,175]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7-q-7","number":"3A","markdown":"Using Gauss Seidel method solve the system of equations\n\n$$\n10x_1 - 2x_2 - x_3 - x_4 = 3\n$$\n\n$$\n-2x_1 + 10x_2 - x_3 - x_4 = 15\n$$\n\n$$\n-x_1 - x_2 + 10x_3 - 2x_4 = 27\n$$\n\n$$\n-x_1 - x_2 - 2x_3 + 10x_4 = -9\n$$\n\nTake the initial approximation as $x_2 = x_3 = x_4 = 0$.\nCarry out 3 iterations and correct up to 4 decimal places.","marks":4,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7/q-7-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1500,1405,314]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7-q-8","number":"3B","markdown":"Solve the differential equation $(D^2 + 1)y = \\sec x \\tan x$ by the method of variation of parameters.","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7/q-8-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1806,1405,73]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7-q-9","number":"3C","markdown":"Compute a real root of $3x - \\cos x - 1 = 0$ using the Newton-Raphson method with $x_0 = 0.6$ correct to four decimal places.","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7/q-9-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,89,1405,130]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7-q-10","number":"4A","markdown":"Using Gram-Schmidt orthogonalization process, construct an orthonormal set of vectors from the set $\\{(1,2,1),\\ (1,0,1),\\ (3,1,0)\\}$ for $\\mathbb{R}^3$.","marks":4,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7/q-10-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,211,1405,145]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7-q-11","number":"4B","markdown":"Solve $(2x + 3)^2 \\dfrac{d^2 y}{dx^2} - (2x + 3) \\dfrac{dy}{dx} - 12y = 6x$.","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7/q-11-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,348,1405,111]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7-q-12","number":"4C","markdown":"Find the eigen values and one of the eigen vectors of the matrix\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix} 8 & -6 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 7 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 \\end{bmatrix}\n$$","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7/q-12-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,451,1405,168],"id":"083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7-q-12-diagram-1","caption":"Matrix A = [[8, -6, 2], [-6, 7, -4], [2, -4, 3]] (original source region)"}],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7/q-12-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,451,1405,168]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7-q-13","number":"5A","markdown":"Define minimal spanning set of vectors. Prove that a minimal spanning set of vectors forms a basis for a vector space $V$ over $F$.","marks":4,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7/q-13-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,611,1405,120]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7-q-14","number":"5B","markdown":"Given $\\dfrac{dy}{dx} = 1 + xy$ with the initial condition $y(0) = 1$. Using Taylor series method, compute $y(0.1)$ correct to four decimal places by considering terms up to fourth order.","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7/q-14-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,723,1405,150]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7-q-15","number":"5C","markdown":"Using the Gauss-Jordan method, find the inverse of:\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7/q-15-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,865,1405,1014],"id":"083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7-q-15-diagram-1","caption":"Matrix A = [[1, 3, 1], [-1, 1, 2], [2, 1, -2]] (original source region)"}],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/083517b4e3e77b1b3dc7/q-15-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,865,1405,1014]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]}],"warnings":["Transcribed from original page images with gpt-5.4-mini. Automatic transcription is not independent human verification."]}
